WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
- My experience of American
food is, sometimes,

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.111
there's strange ingredients.

00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:05.351
So when I try something
new, I get a bit nervous,

00:00:05.351 --> 00:00:07.111
in case it might kill me.

00:00:07.111 --> 00:00:10.832
(fiddle music)

00:00:11.523 --> 00:00:13.868
- Uh, biscuits and gravy
sounds exceptionally weird.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.527
- Biscuit in England
is basically a cookie,

00:00:16.527 --> 00:00:18.432
and gravy is usually what you put on,

00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:20.033
like, mashed potatoes or roast dinner.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.436
So, biscuits and gravy are two things

00:00:22.436 --> 00:00:24.108
that should never be put together.

00:00:24.108 --> 00:00:26.476
- Honestly, it looks like sick.

00:00:26.476 --> 00:00:30.075
- Um, it looks like a cake
with carbonara sauce on it.

00:00:30.075 --> 00:00:32.096
- It smells like car tires.

00:00:32.096 --> 00:00:33.370
- Bottoms up.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.578
(eating sounds)

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.424
- It's horrible.

00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:39.725
- Mmmmm, well.

00:00:39.725 --> 00:00:41.223
- This should be for prisoners!

00:00:41.223 --> 00:00:43.522
- It doesn't taste like anything, really.

00:00:43.522 --> 00:00:46.043
- Salty. That is so salty.

00:00:46.043 --> 00:00:47.969
- It's like, you know that spray you get,

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:49.409
smoke spray you can, like, add to things?

00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:50.421
It's like someone just went like

00:00:50.871 --> 00:00:51.790
all over it.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.860
- I don't, I don't mind
the gravy. It's creamy.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.660
- Yeah, if you just had
the sauce on its own,

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.503
it just tastes like a really
cheap microwave pasta dish.

00:00:58.503 --> 00:00:59.978
But then, you can't ignore

00:00:59.978 --> 00:01:02.234
that 90% of it is the gone-off sponge.

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:04.878
- It's not disgusting.
Like, I don't hate it.

00:01:04.878 --> 00:01:06.445
- I mean, I can see it
probably fills you up.

00:01:06.445 --> 00:01:08.031
If you're hungry, like student food.

00:01:08.031 --> 00:01:09.199
- Maybe Americans would like it.

00:01:09.199 --> 00:01:11.057
I don't think English people
would ever enjoy this,

00:01:11.057 --> 00:01:12.299
especially at breakfast.

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:14.760
- We call these scones, back home,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.616
and you would put jam and cream on them.

00:01:17.616 --> 00:01:19.044
- England has a lot of strange foods

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:20.635
that we think are normal,

00:01:20.635 --> 00:01:22.039
and just coming out to America,

00:01:22.039 --> 00:01:25.336
I realize how strange our
cuisine seems to people.

00:01:25.336 --> 00:01:27.414
- This is not something
I would seek out again.

00:01:27.414 --> 00:01:29.643
It doesn't taste amazing.

00:01:29.643 --> 00:01:32.801
Um, but I can imagine, if
you've grown up with it,

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.115
it would give you a sense of comfort.

00:01:34.115 --> 00:01:35.555
It is that comfort food.

00:01:35.555 --> 00:01:37.610
- And, it doesn't make sense in my brain,

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.175
because we grew up with
something completely different.

00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:41.777
So, it's just a cultural difference,

00:01:41.777 --> 00:01:44.250
and we shouldn't really
be too mean about it.

00:01:47.105 --> 00:01:49.149
- It's just so sad, what's
happening over there.

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:50.461
- Oh, yeah, mm-hmm. (whoosh of air)

00:01:50.461 --> 00:01:53.224
(drum solo music)

00:01:53.224 --> 00:01:54.908
You don't know the half of it.

00:01:54.908 --> 00:01:57.656
(calm piano music)

